{"study_accession":"PRJNA765133","secondary_study_accession":"SRP338221","title":"Gene expression analyses of EBV-immortalized B cells from patients with MS and controls","description":"The immunopathogenic occurrence of multiple sclerosis (MS) is thought to be triggered by en-vironmental factors in individuals with an unfavorable genetic predisposition. There is striking evidence, that Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) infection is a major risk factor in later development of MS. Human endogenous retroviruses (HERV) are suggested to be the missing link in the de-layed development of MS as they can be transactivated by EBV. In the present study, we have investigated differential gene expression pattern in MS and controls after latent EBV-infection of B cells in lymphoblastoid cell lines (LCL).","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":16,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN21544042","study_accession":"PRJNA765133","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"PBMC_MS donor 10","description":"PBMC_MS donor 10","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-11-09","attributes":[["isolate","PBMC_MS donor 10"],["age","35"],["biomaterial_provider","Lisa Wieland and Martin S. Staege, University Clinic Halle (Saale), Ernst-Grube-Street 40, 06097 Halle (Saale), Germany"],["sex","female"],["tissue","peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["disease","multiple sclerosis"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR16011118","experiment_accession":"SRX12298048","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"unspecified","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":31651199,"base_count":9495359700,"first_public":"2021-11-09","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: RNAseq of PBMC_MS donor 10"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN21544043","study_accession":"PRJNA765133","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"PBMC_MS donor 13","description":"PBMC_MS donor 13","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access"